1
00:00:17,910 --> 00:00:20,380
(Kang Hoon, Cho Hyun Chul, Kim Jeong Jin)

2
00:00:23,610 --> 00:00:25,620
(Lee E Dam, Moon Hee, Yoon Ga I)

3
00:00:33,520 --> 00:00:35,060
(Jeon Bae Soo, Lee Seo Hwan, Oh Eui Sik)

4
00:00:54,980 --> 00:00:57,350
(Happy Anding)

5
00:00:57,350 --> 00:00:59,020
(This program contains indirect advertisements.)

6
00:00:59,020 --> 00:01:00,250
(All people, groups, firms, places, and events are fictional.)

7
00:01:00,250 --> 00:01:01,450
(Child actors were filmed safely with their guardians present.)

8
00:01:01,450 --> 00:01:02,650
(Animal scenes were staged under welfare rules.)

9
00:01:02,650 --> 00:01:03,850
(AI-based technology was used in parts of the production.)

10
00:01:04,960 --> 00:01:07,630
(3 months ago)

11
00:01:09,930 --> 00:01:11,960
If you're upset about something, tell me.

12
00:01:11,960 --> 00:01:13,600
Get it off your chest, Jun Seo.

13
00:01:14,060 --> 00:01:16,770
- I told you, I'm not. - You're driving me crazy.

14
00:01:18,340 --> 00:01:20,600
Is this because I used too much hot water?

15
00:01:21,970 --> 00:01:22,970
Yes.

16
00:01:23,040 --> 00:01:24,580
Comedy begins with observation.

17
00:01:26,410 --> 00:01:27,810
Wherever there are people,

18
00:01:27,810 --> 00:01:29,750
there are as many characters as there are faces.

19
00:01:31,680 --> 00:01:33,020
Their outward appearance.

20
00:01:34,920 --> 00:01:36,990
The secret tastes hidden within.

21
00:01:38,920 --> 00:01:40,690
The personality traits that slip out moment by moment.

22
00:01:43,490 --> 00:01:45,930
Those things come together to create a single character.

23
00:01:46,600 --> 00:01:48,270
(Asura)

24
00:01:48,330 --> 00:01:49,470
I find that fascinating.

25
00:01:49,830 --> 00:01:53,240
(The Perfect Cleaning Experts: Clean Team)

26
00:02:02,710 --> 00:02:05,020
Did you cut your hair? I thought you were in high school.

27
00:02:09,590 --> 00:02:11,860
Three iced Americanos, please.

28
00:02:15,060 --> 00:02:18,100
Still, she could at least say hello back.

29
00:02:20,600 --> 00:02:22,400
The most fascinating moment of all is...

30
00:02:23,730 --> 00:02:24,840
"Thank you."

31
00:02:29,370 --> 00:02:33,180
"Thanks for the compliment." "Three iced Americanos, right?"

32
00:02:36,510 --> 00:02:37,780
Is that so hard?

33
00:02:39,750 --> 00:02:40,750
Idiot.

34
00:02:41,690 --> 00:02:43,290
Hey, we have a big group.

35
00:02:57,900 --> 00:02:59,740
When you catch a glimpse of a hidden side...

36
00:02:59,740 --> 00:03:01,410
in someone you thought you had all figured out.

37
00:03:05,410 --> 00:03:08,380
That's when real observation begins.

38
00:03:15,090 --> 00:03:16,120
What's visible...

39
00:03:20,720 --> 00:03:21,760
Welcome.

40
00:03:22,360 --> 00:03:23,460
And what's not.

41
00:03:25,500 --> 00:03:28,200
- It's so hot. - So hot.

42
00:03:28,530 --> 00:03:30,670
- It's blazing today, right? - Yes, it is.

43
00:03:31,240 --> 00:03:33,700
What do you have here for kids to drink?

44
00:03:33,800 --> 00:03:36,810
For our kids' menu, we have peach juice, orange juice,

45
00:03:36,870 --> 00:03:39,240
mango juice, and chocolate chip. Four choices in all.

46
00:03:40,480 --> 00:03:44,520
One mango juice and one iced Americano, please.

47
00:04:05,100 --> 00:04:06,140
And before you know it,

48
00:04:08,870 --> 00:04:11,340
that person starts to occupy every corner of your mind.

49
00:04:12,480 --> 00:04:15,380
No, but seriously, she genuinely creeps me out so much...

50
00:04:15,380 --> 00:04:16,850
that I can't focus on our meeting.

51
00:04:18,420 --> 00:04:20,080
Her default face is literally like this.

52
00:04:23,720 --> 00:04:26,360
Hey, how about a character like this?

53
00:04:26,990 --> 00:04:28,090
The title is...

54
00:04:28,990 --> 00:04:30,260
"Woman with a Twist."

55
00:04:34,470 --> 00:04:37,870
(New Asura Video)

56
00:04:48,250 --> 00:04:51,780
That's the exact moment a new character is born.

57
00:04:52,450 --> 00:04:53,820
Today is my first day on the job...

58
00:04:54,790 --> 00:04:56,250
Forget the timid me from yesterday.

59
00:04:56,920 --> 00:04:58,490
I'm going to be reborn as a whole new person.

60
00:04:59,390 --> 00:05:00,560
Let's do this.

61
00:05:01,090 --> 00:05:02,090
Let's do this.

62
00:05:02,690 --> 00:05:04,960
Oh, no, what do I do?

63
00:05:07,030 --> 00:05:08,230
And that's why a comedian...

64
00:05:09,700 --> 00:05:11,140
can't help but fall in love...

65
00:05:14,140 --> 00:05:15,770
with the characters they create.

66
00:05:15,840 --> 00:05:17,980
(Episode 5: It's a Romantic Comedy)

67
00:05:25,880 --> 00:05:27,280
(Soojung Villa)

68
00:05:44,030 --> 00:05:46,870
I got it. I got the internship.

69
00:05:48,140 --> 00:05:50,570
This was the company I really wanted to work for.

70
00:05:50,870 --> 00:05:54,380
Today is the happiest day of my whole life.

71
00:06:01,250 --> 00:06:02,250
Excuse me.

72
00:06:02,890 --> 00:06:04,860
(Soojung Villa)

73
00:06:05,460 --> 00:06:06,460
Hey.

74
00:06:20,540 --> 00:06:21,540
I'm so sorry.

75
00:06:21,740 --> 00:06:23,240
(Soojung Villa)

76
00:06:33,650 --> 00:06:34,690
Well...

77
00:06:39,760 --> 00:06:42,060
(Soojung Villa)

78
00:06:44,560 --> 00:06:46,300
I'm sorry. I'm so sorry.

79
00:06:46,500 --> 00:06:49,800
No, I'm the one who should apologize.

80
00:06:51,870 --> 00:06:53,970
I heard you called off the disbandment,

81
00:06:54,710 --> 00:06:55,710
and I was just so happy.

82
00:06:57,570 --> 00:06:59,410
Right... Yes.

83
00:07:02,110 --> 00:07:03,180
That's wonderful.

84
00:07:04,550 --> 00:07:05,580
What are you doing?

85
00:07:09,320 --> 00:07:10,690
How beautiful. How very beautiful.

86
00:07:12,020 --> 00:07:16,460
Don't stop on our account. It's so nice to see.

87
00:07:16,530 --> 00:07:20,830
Eun Young, you're so busted. I'm telling Mom everything.

88
00:07:25,870 --> 00:07:26,870
What are you looking at, man?

89
00:07:31,480 --> 00:07:32,480
Nice.

90
00:07:33,040 --> 00:07:34,040
I love you.

91
00:07:34,440 --> 00:07:35,450
I love you too.

92
00:07:41,420 --> 00:07:43,620
I thought I was watching a movie.

93
00:07:44,620 --> 00:07:47,590
You know what they say. "Still waters run deep."

94
00:07:47,660 --> 00:07:50,390
I haven't even grazed Jun Seo's fingertips,

95
00:07:50,390 --> 00:07:52,900
and here you are, leaping into a guy's arms in broad daylight.

96
00:07:52,960 --> 00:07:55,600
Hey. When did I do that?

97
00:07:55,600 --> 00:07:56,800
Come on, be honest.

98
00:07:57,770 --> 00:08:00,040
- Is there something going on? - What are you talking about?

99
00:08:01,070 --> 00:08:05,380
- I was just really happy. - "Happy"?

100
00:08:05,780 --> 00:08:09,150
You hug like this, all tangled up, just because you're happy?

101
00:08:09,480 --> 00:08:13,080
That was no celebratory hug. That was a romantic hug.

102
00:08:13,250 --> 00:08:15,390
If you're going to talk nonsense, get out. Get out!

103
00:08:15,390 --> 00:08:17,920
Wait, wait. Just let me ask you one thing, then.

104
00:08:18,290 --> 00:08:21,120
I really want you to be honest with me.

105
00:08:23,830 --> 00:08:25,530
Earlier, when Tae Gu held you,

106
00:08:27,200 --> 00:08:28,200
did it feel good?

107
00:08:28,670 --> 00:08:30,770
- I bet it did. - Get out. Get out.

108
00:08:30,830 --> 00:08:31,840
It did, didn't it?

109
00:08:33,470 --> 00:08:34,470
Get out!

110
00:08:34,770 --> 00:08:37,170
Darn it, what are we going to do? We're in big trouble, seriously.

111
00:08:37,240 --> 00:08:38,380
No, seriously.

112
00:08:38,940 --> 00:08:40,980
Since when did it start?

113
00:08:41,110 --> 00:08:44,280
Hey, since when were you two a thing?

114
00:08:44,350 --> 00:08:46,080
Come on, spill it.

115
00:08:46,150 --> 00:08:48,790
Stop spitting! You're ruining my food.

116
00:08:50,350 --> 00:08:52,520
Where are you going? Finish eating. Look at him running away.

117
00:08:52,520 --> 00:08:53,560
You're acting shady.

118
00:08:53,560 --> 00:08:54,960
There's something going on, isn't there?

119
00:08:55,790 --> 00:08:57,030
We're right.

120
00:08:57,460 --> 00:08:58,900
Give it a rest, seriously.

121
00:08:59,560 --> 00:09:01,060
It was just a hug.

122
00:09:01,130 --> 00:09:02,570
Are you in grade school? You're so childish.

123
00:09:02,630 --> 00:09:04,400
Yes, I'm in grade school, you jerk.

124
00:09:05,270 --> 00:09:07,740
"Just a hug"? I don't think so.

125
00:09:07,840 --> 00:09:09,840
There was definitely something in your eyes.

126
00:09:09,940 --> 00:09:11,540
Right? He looked weird, didn't he?

127
00:09:11,610 --> 00:09:13,610
Man, the look in your eyes was totally suspicious.

128
00:09:13,840 --> 00:09:14,850
See?

129
00:09:21,790 --> 00:09:24,220
What would you have done if we weren't there?

130
00:09:24,220 --> 00:09:25,390
What am I going to do, seriously?

131
00:09:26,790 --> 00:09:28,530
Whatever, it's not like that, you idiot.

132
00:09:29,090 --> 00:09:30,830
Do I look like I have time to date someone right now?

133
00:09:30,890 --> 00:09:32,300
I barely have enough time to write our sketches.

134
00:09:32,430 --> 00:09:35,370
Changing the subject by acting pissed off, are we?

135
00:09:36,270 --> 00:09:37,770
- Hey. - Yes, totally.

136
00:09:37,830 --> 00:09:40,770
Shut up. Next week, we have a review,

137
00:09:40,770 --> 00:09:43,040
so go to the cafe as soon as you wake up to brainstorm.

138
00:09:43,140 --> 00:09:44,680
- Yes, sir. - I'll join you as fast as I can.

139
00:09:45,080 --> 00:09:46,640
- Understood. - Where are you going?

140
00:09:47,140 --> 00:09:48,550
Before we start over,

141
00:09:49,310 --> 00:09:50,610
there's something I have to take care of.

142
00:09:53,180 --> 00:09:54,250
Hey, she's watching your back.

143
00:09:54,380 --> 00:09:55,390
- Hello. - Hey.

144
00:09:55,450 --> 00:09:56,820
- Just kidding. - Oh, come on.

145
00:09:57,120 --> 00:09:58,390
- Cut it out! - Just kidding.

146
00:09:59,220 --> 00:10:00,360
It's not like that!

147
00:10:03,660 --> 00:10:04,830
Darn it, that's hot.

148
00:10:14,140 --> 00:10:15,310
Isn't it lunchtime?

149
00:10:22,380 --> 00:10:23,950
How much money are you trying to scrape together...

150
00:10:24,010 --> 00:10:25,250
that you're skipping meals to work?

151
00:10:26,080 --> 00:10:27,450
This is the fruit stand guy's car, right?

152
00:10:27,990 --> 00:10:29,390
Did he bring it, pretending he was just passing by,

153
00:10:29,450 --> 00:10:30,590
and sneakily leave it here again?

154
00:10:31,920 --> 00:10:34,260
I told you to stop fixing things for free like that.

155
00:10:34,730 --> 00:10:36,390
That guy charges me full price for fruit.

156
00:10:36,490 --> 00:10:38,560
Stop pretending things are fine and go inside.

157
00:10:39,430 --> 00:10:40,530
Your brother is inside.

158
00:10:42,870 --> 00:10:44,530
Busted.

159
00:10:56,810 --> 00:10:57,810
Dad, you know...

160
00:11:00,120 --> 00:11:01,550
I actually came to see you today.

161
00:11:03,050 --> 00:11:04,290
There's something I want to tell you.

162
00:11:16,230 --> 00:11:17,230
Dad.

163
00:11:19,570 --> 00:11:21,170
I've decided to keep doing comedy.

164
00:11:22,870 --> 00:11:23,970
I'm not going to give up.

165
00:11:25,880 --> 00:11:27,140
You were probably hoping...

166
00:11:27,140 --> 00:11:28,610
I was finally going to make something of myself,

167
00:11:30,480 --> 00:11:31,780
so I guess I still have a long way to go.

168
00:11:34,050 --> 00:11:35,050
I'm sorry.

169
00:11:37,520 --> 00:11:38,660
But Dad, the thing is...

170
00:11:44,030 --> 00:11:45,030
I...

171
00:11:50,370 --> 00:11:51,740
I love comedy so much.

172
00:11:57,940 --> 00:11:59,580
I tried to quit, but...

173
00:12:02,050 --> 00:12:03,050
I can't.

174
00:12:04,450 --> 00:12:05,650
I just can't bring myself to do it.

175
00:12:08,520 --> 00:12:10,650
For now, I don't think I can live without comedy.

176
00:12:13,120 --> 00:12:14,160
So...

177
00:12:18,260 --> 00:12:20,160
could you please cut me some slack?

178
00:12:23,600 --> 00:12:25,740
I'm really going to give it everything I have this time.

179
00:12:28,210 --> 00:12:29,710
So when I finally make it...

180
00:12:32,240 --> 00:12:33,310
just once...

181
00:12:35,410 --> 00:12:36,610
with my own performance...

182
00:12:40,020 --> 00:12:41,750
I want to earn your approval.

183
00:12:59,440 --> 00:13:00,770
They were on sale, so I picked them up.

184
00:13:04,410 --> 00:13:06,840
Don't stash them away just because you're mad at me.

185
00:13:08,550 --> 00:13:09,550
Please use them.

186
00:13:13,980 --> 00:13:15,790
I'll get going, Dad.

187
00:13:30,100 --> 00:13:31,100
Dad.

188
00:13:32,140 --> 00:13:33,340
Dad, wasn't that Tae Gu?

189
00:13:35,010 --> 00:13:36,210
That rude little punk.

190
00:13:36,270 --> 00:13:37,440
He didn't even say hello to his own brother.

191
00:13:37,510 --> 00:13:38,710
He says he's doing comedy again.

192
00:13:40,940 --> 00:13:42,150
He came by just to tell me that.

193
00:13:43,210 --> 00:13:44,210
Really?

194
00:13:46,380 --> 00:13:47,680
I'm going to take a short break,

195
00:13:48,750 --> 00:13:50,320
so clean this up for me.

196
00:13:51,020 --> 00:13:52,020
Sure.

197
00:13:52,420 --> 00:13:55,760
Get some good rest, Dad. I'll clean up everything. Don't worry.

198
00:13:58,560 --> 00:13:59,800
That kid.

199
00:14:00,960 --> 00:14:02,100
If he was going to do this anyway,

200
00:14:02,100 --> 00:14:03,430
he didn't have to make us worry so much.

201
00:14:27,120 --> 00:14:28,260
That brat.

202
00:14:29,730 --> 00:14:31,560
Who sells out their own family at a discount?

203
00:14:49,210 --> 00:14:50,680
Why does it have to be this hard?

204
00:14:54,680 --> 00:14:55,690
Eun Hye.

205
00:14:57,590 --> 00:15:00,960
(Eunhye Auto Repair Shop, Grand Reopening Special Discount)

206
00:15:07,660 --> 00:15:09,730
Sample job interview questions.

207
00:15:10,470 --> 00:15:11,470
(A Resume Guaranteed to Pass)

208
00:15:11,770 --> 00:15:12,900
Okay.

209
00:15:17,510 --> 00:15:18,510
Nam Il.

210
00:15:19,610 --> 00:15:21,010
Hey, you're here?

211
00:15:23,350 --> 00:15:25,320
Am I late? I had to stop somewhere first.

212
00:15:25,580 --> 00:15:26,580
It's fine.

213
00:15:39,730 --> 00:15:41,000
Why do you look so frozen?

214
00:15:43,730 --> 00:15:45,140
Because of that bad interview?

215
00:15:47,000 --> 00:15:50,070
It's okay. It would be weirder if you passed on the first try.

216
00:15:52,240 --> 00:15:54,380
- Actually, I... - Na Yeon.

217
00:16:06,860 --> 00:16:08,190
I want to keep doing comedy.

218
00:16:15,630 --> 00:16:17,600
If I give up like this,

219
00:16:18,600 --> 00:16:21,400
I feel like I'll regret it for the rest of my life.

220
00:16:26,110 --> 00:16:27,480
I'm sorry. I'm so sorry.

221
00:16:35,350 --> 00:16:36,490
Is that all?

222
00:16:39,290 --> 00:16:40,290
What?

223
00:16:48,870 --> 00:16:50,770
What was that?

224
00:16:50,770 --> 00:16:51,970
You were being so serious that...

225
00:16:51,970 --> 00:16:54,200
I thought you were cheating on me or something.

226
00:16:58,540 --> 00:16:59,780
You're not disappointed?

227
00:17:00,380 --> 00:17:02,310
If you want to do it, you should.

228
00:17:02,380 --> 00:17:03,950
What do you have to be sorry to me for?

229
00:17:05,150 --> 00:17:06,750
You held out longer than I thought, Kim Nam Il.

230
00:17:16,690 --> 00:17:19,000
I'm such a lucky guy.

231
00:17:21,400 --> 00:17:23,530
Na Yeon, thank you so much.

232
00:17:29,140 --> 00:17:30,470
You worked hard.

233
00:17:40,920 --> 00:17:43,820
He must think I'm weird, right?

234
00:18:02,940 --> 00:18:04,310
Are the guys not here yet?

235
00:18:06,480 --> 00:18:09,780
- No. - I told those jerks to come early.

236
00:18:14,580 --> 00:18:15,750
Hey, wait...

237
00:18:16,820 --> 00:18:19,490
You were really startled yesterday, weren't you?

238
00:18:20,120 --> 00:18:22,130
I'm so sorry. I'm not usually the type...

239
00:18:22,890 --> 00:18:27,830
to just grab onto someone like that.

240
00:18:31,670 --> 00:18:33,070
I just...

241
00:18:33,770 --> 00:18:37,240
I just wanted to make sure in case you took it the wrong way.

242
00:18:38,140 --> 00:18:40,540
It's not like I have any special feelings...

243
00:18:40,540 --> 00:18:42,010
or romantic intentions toward you, Tae Gu.

244
00:18:42,080 --> 00:18:43,210
You know that, right?

245
00:18:45,620 --> 00:18:47,180
Yes.

246
00:18:51,090 --> 00:18:55,160
I really just did that as a pure fan.

247
00:18:56,290 --> 00:18:58,430
I had zero ulterior motives...

248
00:19:00,400 --> 00:19:02,200
- I know, me too. - Really, I mean it.

249
00:19:02,270 --> 00:19:06,270
I swear to the skies, I don't have the slightest...

250
00:19:07,740 --> 00:19:10,210
I get it. How many times are you going to say it?

251
00:19:10,810 --> 00:19:12,310
What? You're here already?

252
00:19:13,340 --> 00:19:14,340
Why are you so early?

253
00:19:14,640 --> 00:19:16,380
Why did you crawl in so late, you jerk?

254
00:19:16,750 --> 00:19:18,050
Why are you snapping at us?

255
00:19:18,410 --> 00:19:19,420
Why are you...

256
00:19:19,880 --> 00:19:22,050
- Hello. - Hello.

257
00:19:23,650 --> 00:19:24,650
Do you know what time it is?

258
00:19:26,220 --> 00:19:28,160
He gets here early and takes it out on us.

259
00:19:28,220 --> 00:19:29,230
Tell me about it.

260
00:19:33,060 --> 00:19:34,300
Why are you so mad?

261
00:19:39,870 --> 00:19:42,340
It's on the house. You need full bellies...

262
00:19:42,610 --> 00:19:44,470
to come up with good ideas.

263
00:19:44,910 --> 00:19:46,040
- Thank you. - Thank you.

264
00:19:46,110 --> 00:19:47,540
See? The only person who looks out for us...

265
00:19:47,640 --> 00:19:49,250
is our president.

266
00:19:49,480 --> 00:19:51,380
President?

267
00:19:51,380 --> 00:19:55,520
Eun Young, you have become our fan club president.

268
00:19:56,390 --> 00:19:57,390
Pardon?

269
00:19:58,820 --> 00:19:59,820
That's ridiculous.

270
00:19:59,890 --> 00:20:01,990
Who am I to be anything like a president?

271
00:20:02,560 --> 00:20:05,800
Just a second. Hold on. Wait right there.

272
00:20:09,630 --> 00:20:10,930
All right, attention.

273
00:20:11,670 --> 00:20:13,100
Eyes on me. Attention.

274
00:20:15,640 --> 00:20:16,710
Certificate of Appointment.

275
00:20:17,240 --> 00:20:19,040
Name, Go Eun Young.

276
00:20:19,340 --> 00:20:23,450
As a steadfast supporter of Asura and our dear friend,

277
00:20:23,480 --> 00:20:25,980
you have contributed greatly to Asura's continued existence.

278
00:20:26,120 --> 00:20:27,680
In recognition of your dedication,

279
00:20:27,750 --> 00:20:30,650
we hereby appoint you as the president of Asura's fan club.

280
00:20:30,720 --> 00:20:31,720
Are you five?

281
00:20:32,190 --> 00:20:33,390
Congratulations.

282
00:20:33,690 --> 00:20:36,390
- I love it so much. - This is just temporary.

283
00:20:36,460 --> 00:20:37,990
Later on, we'll get a gold border...

284
00:20:38,060 --> 00:20:39,800
and put it in a proper frame for you.

285
00:20:39,860 --> 00:20:41,800
No, this is more than enough.

286
00:20:44,070 --> 00:20:45,600
Go ahead with your meeting.

287
00:20:46,300 --> 00:20:48,440
Just let me know if you need anything else.

288
00:20:48,840 --> 00:20:50,340
- Thank you. - Thank you, Madam President.

289
00:20:50,410 --> 00:20:51,870
Thank you, Madam President. Love you.

290
00:20:51,940 --> 00:20:53,080
Thank you, Madam President.

291
00:20:53,440 --> 00:20:55,040
Watch your step on the stairs.

292
00:20:55,480 --> 00:20:57,780
Hey, come on. Can you stop teasing her?

293
00:20:57,850 --> 00:20:59,320
She likes it, so what's your problem?

294
00:20:59,380 --> 00:21:01,720
Yes, Madam President is happy with it.

295
00:21:01,780 --> 00:21:03,020
Who are you to get mad?

296
00:21:03,220 --> 00:21:05,050
Forget it, all right? Just get back to the meeting.

297
00:21:05,150 --> 00:21:06,390
A gift from our president.

298
00:21:22,440 --> 00:21:23,570
Hey, focus, focus.

299
00:21:23,940 --> 00:21:25,110
- Focusing. - I'm focused.

300
00:21:25,110 --> 00:21:27,040
- Hey, we didn't even eat any of it! - You said you'd write your part.

301
00:21:27,110 --> 00:21:28,880
- Work on your material yourself. - You can't finish that anyway.

302
00:21:29,110 --> 00:21:31,410
Boxers who can dodge, dodge everything.

303
00:21:31,480 --> 00:21:33,020
Let me match your pace...

304
00:21:37,250 --> 00:21:38,990
There's not enough time to explain this...

305
00:21:39,060 --> 00:21:40,190
We need to wash this...

306
00:21:40,260 --> 00:21:41,320
There's something we have to wash.

307
00:21:44,260 --> 00:21:46,560
Right, okay. Did you rinse it with water?

308
00:21:47,900 --> 00:21:49,430
- We're sorry. - Sorry about that.

309
00:21:50,500 --> 00:21:51,500
That's it.

310
00:21:53,840 --> 00:21:54,840
Are you really pouring it in your ear?

311
00:21:55,040 --> 00:21:56,040
I'm sorry...

312
00:21:56,710 --> 00:21:57,710
Sorry.

313
00:21:58,440 --> 00:22:01,540
- Thank you. - Hey. No, how I move...

314
00:22:02,550 --> 00:22:04,680
- Hey. - If you keep pulling,

315
00:22:04,750 --> 00:22:06,080
- what do you expect me to do? - Just let go then.

316
00:22:06,220 --> 00:22:08,450
At that exact moment, take off the sunglasses,

317
00:22:08,520 --> 00:22:10,520
and underneath is a giant black eye...

318
00:22:11,520 --> 00:22:13,260
What prehistoric slapstick bit is this?

319
00:22:13,420 --> 00:22:14,890
Why not draw on some snot while you're at it?

320
00:22:14,960 --> 00:22:16,560
You idiot. It's a classic. A classic, man.

321
00:22:16,630 --> 00:22:19,200
- Don't you know what a classic is? - Classic my foot.

322
00:22:19,260 --> 00:22:20,630
It's just not funny.

323
00:22:20,700 --> 00:22:21,930
Then you plug the cord into the nose,

324
00:22:22,000 --> 00:22:23,070
and boom, it starts charging.

325
00:22:25,130 --> 00:22:26,240
It's not funny.

326
00:22:26,240 --> 00:22:27,540
I hate classics.

327
00:22:27,670 --> 00:22:29,210
I said I'm not doing classics.

328
00:22:29,270 --> 00:22:31,710
Let's go with something trendy instead.

329
00:22:31,770 --> 00:22:36,180
No, just do it like this, just try it like this for once.

330
00:22:39,180 --> 00:22:41,380
Look, look. See this? Look at him.

331
00:22:41,450 --> 00:22:44,520
- This guy is laughing. - I think it's funny!

332
00:22:45,820 --> 00:22:49,190
I said it's funny, you bastards. It's funny!

333
00:22:49,260 --> 00:22:51,690
Both of you are funny. Tae Gu, Nam Il!

334
00:22:51,760 --> 00:22:53,800
You're the funniest guys in the world!

335
00:22:56,400 --> 00:22:57,670
All right, man.

336
00:22:59,740 --> 00:23:01,440
What's with you today? Did something happen?

337
00:23:01,740 --> 00:23:04,570
You guys really are the funniest in the world.

338
00:23:05,480 --> 00:23:06,510
I'm sorry.

339
00:23:07,010 --> 00:23:08,880
(Man Sik's Skewers)

340
00:23:40,340 --> 00:23:41,340
Is this it?

341
00:23:42,110 --> 00:23:45,080
Yes, that's it. A lifesaver.

342
00:23:45,150 --> 00:23:46,750
- A lifesaver. - Thank you.

343
00:23:46,820 --> 00:23:47,820
Glad to help.

344
00:23:48,520 --> 00:23:50,250
By the way, why are you alone today?

345
00:23:50,690 --> 00:23:52,090
Jun Seo said he needed to test out...

346
00:23:52,160 --> 00:23:54,460
a new routine at the theater, so I told him to go ahead.

347
00:23:54,520 --> 00:23:56,230
- And the other guy vanished. - What?

348
00:23:58,900 --> 00:24:00,900
(Asura)

349
00:24:03,200 --> 00:24:05,540
Still, the guys are really lucky.

350
00:24:05,840 --> 00:24:08,540
Having such a generous teacher and mentor like you.

351
00:24:09,740 --> 00:24:10,970
Who's giving what? Me?

352
00:24:11,340 --> 00:24:12,640
Do I look like the giving type to you?

353
00:24:12,740 --> 00:24:13,740
Yes.

354
00:24:15,950 --> 00:24:17,980
Have you heard the saying that you only know...

355
00:24:18,050 --> 00:24:20,350
who your real people are once you hit rock bottom?

356
00:24:26,660 --> 00:24:28,420
He got fired? All of a sudden?

357
00:24:28,690 --> 00:24:29,960
The chairman only picked kids...

358
00:24:29,960 --> 00:24:31,490
from families that donated to be class presidents,

359
00:24:31,560 --> 00:24:33,600
and he rebelled because he couldn't stand it.

360
00:24:33,800 --> 00:24:35,400
He dug his own grave.

361
00:24:35,570 --> 00:24:37,600
Does he think others keep quiet because they can't speak up?

362
00:24:45,340 --> 00:24:46,340
Hey.

363
00:24:46,940 --> 00:24:48,010
Man Sik...

364
00:25:03,990 --> 00:25:05,660
Even though I was head of student affairs,

365
00:25:05,730 --> 00:25:07,430
all those people who hung around me...

366
00:25:07,500 --> 00:25:08,900
and chuckled with me until yesterday...

367
00:25:08,970 --> 00:25:11,830
Not a single one of them showed up. But right then,

368
00:25:14,870 --> 00:25:15,870
Mr. Jung.

369
00:25:22,650 --> 00:25:24,010
Those kids showed up.

370
00:25:43,530 --> 00:25:44,670
Please eat something.

371
00:25:55,510 --> 00:25:58,480
(Yeongwon Memorial Park)

372
00:26:25,880 --> 00:26:27,410
What's he wearing?

373
00:26:31,880 --> 00:26:32,880
I'm sorry.

374
00:26:33,080 --> 00:26:35,920
He didn't have a suit, so he nicked it from the prop room.

375
00:26:41,890 --> 00:26:44,330
What am I going to do with you fools?

376
00:26:48,560 --> 00:26:50,100
Seriously, you look so ugly.

377
00:26:54,640 --> 00:26:56,110
Are you laughing or crying?

378
00:26:57,270 --> 00:27:01,140
You're creeping us out, sir. Take a photo. Capture an ugly one.

379
00:27:01,210 --> 00:27:03,110
- What are you doing? - One, two, three.

380
00:27:03,280 --> 00:27:04,580
Don't take it.

381
00:27:04,950 --> 00:27:06,820
- Three. - Don't take it, you jerks.

382
00:27:06,880 --> 00:27:08,350
- One, two, three. - Cry again. Come on, cry again.

383
00:27:08,420 --> 00:27:09,920
Who's crying, you little punks?

384
00:27:10,190 --> 00:27:12,290
- Look over here. - That's just how they are.

385
00:27:13,160 --> 00:27:14,620
When I'm with those guys,

386
00:27:15,160 --> 00:27:17,530
they drive me crazy, but I'm never lonely.

387
00:27:17,730 --> 00:27:21,260
That's why I stick by them through thick and thin.

388
00:27:25,130 --> 00:27:27,500
My sister actually said the same thing.

389
00:27:28,000 --> 00:27:30,910
She said watching them warms her heart.

390
00:27:32,880 --> 00:27:34,780
They're really good kids.

391
00:27:35,340 --> 00:27:38,310
So I hope all their hard work finally pays off this time.

392
00:27:40,320 --> 00:27:43,890
(To Man Sik's Skewers, Asura)

393
00:27:44,690 --> 00:27:46,160
- Did you grab everything? - Yes.

394
00:27:46,220 --> 00:27:47,490
Look at this crowd. So many people.

395
00:27:48,220 --> 00:27:50,130
All right, everyone. Come join us.

396
00:27:50,130 --> 00:27:52,360
We're Asura, and right now,

397
00:27:52,430 --> 00:27:53,900
we're going to promote our comedy show.

398
00:27:53,960 --> 00:27:56,030
- Is this all you brought? - Right here by our side,

399
00:27:56,100 --> 00:27:58,200
you can watch it happen live, right before your eyes.

400
00:27:58,270 --> 00:27:59,800
Yes, let's go.

401
00:28:00,640 --> 00:28:02,510
Just one more person... Wait, two more...

402
00:28:02,870 --> 00:28:04,070
I think we should just start.

403
00:28:04,510 --> 00:28:05,740
- Hello, everyone. We are... - Wait, hold on...

404
00:28:05,810 --> 00:28:06,810
We're here to turn your minds...

405
00:28:06,880 --> 00:28:08,280
Into total chaos...

406
00:28:08,340 --> 00:28:09,350
- We're Asura! - We're Asura!

407
00:28:11,510 --> 00:28:12,520
- We're Asura. - Asura!

408
00:28:12,580 --> 00:28:13,720
- We're Asura. - Thank you.

409
00:28:13,780 --> 00:28:17,120
All right. In just a moment, Asura's comedy show will begin.

410
00:28:17,120 --> 00:28:18,150
Thank you.

411
00:28:18,220 --> 00:28:19,560
- Thank you. - Come see our show.

412
00:28:19,560 --> 00:28:21,490
Asura's comedy show is starting soon.

413
00:28:21,560 --> 00:28:22,560
- It's hilarious. - Where are you going?

414
00:28:22,890 --> 00:28:25,660
- Let me guess. - Shows are at three and six.

415
00:28:25,730 --> 00:28:28,500
- Bring all your friends. - Asura.

416
00:28:28,560 --> 00:28:31,030
Excuse me, where are you headed in such a rush?

417
00:28:34,340 --> 00:28:36,640
- Asura is putting on a show! - Do you like comedy?

418
00:28:36,710 --> 00:28:37,740
Come visit our theater.

419
00:28:38,510 --> 00:28:39,640
- Hello. - Over here.

420
00:28:39,710 --> 00:28:40,710
What's this?

421
00:28:40,710 --> 00:28:41,740
(Live Chatting)

422
00:28:41,740 --> 00:28:42,750
(Report Message)

423
00:28:43,310 --> 00:28:44,610
(Harassment or Violence)

424
00:28:44,950 --> 00:28:47,420
Come check out our show.

425
00:28:47,480 --> 00:28:50,820
Asura is performing today. Thank you.

426
00:28:54,660 --> 00:28:57,260
- Shows at three and six. - I'm home.

427
00:28:58,660 --> 00:29:00,430
Look at that smile.

428
00:29:00,900 --> 00:29:02,470
Did you even eat while watching that?

429
00:29:04,030 --> 00:29:06,070
I don't need food. My heart is full.

430
00:29:06,070 --> 00:29:07,540
Come watch us perform.

431
00:29:07,540 --> 00:29:09,070
Don't they look so happy?

432
00:29:09,070 --> 00:29:11,410
- Comedy show today. Thank you. - The three of them really...

433
00:29:11,510 --> 00:29:14,040
shine the brightest when they're in front of a crowd.

434
00:29:14,340 --> 00:29:15,580
They just sparkle.

435
00:29:15,980 --> 00:29:18,180
- It's hilarious. - This is truly touching.

436
00:29:18,250 --> 00:29:19,250
A devoted fangirl's true love.

437
00:29:20,920 --> 00:29:23,520
Excuse me, but I'm not just any regular fangirl anymore.

438
00:29:23,820 --> 00:29:25,750
- I'm the fan club president. - What?

439
00:29:25,890 --> 00:29:27,490
- Hello. - Come watch our show.

440
00:29:27,560 --> 00:29:31,490
A reliable sponsor and friend of Asura.

441
00:29:31,560 --> 00:29:33,400
- What? - They said so.

442
00:29:33,400 --> 00:29:34,930
Goodness.

443
00:29:35,089 --> 00:29:36,859
Forgive me for not recognizing your greatness.

444
00:29:36,929 --> 00:29:37,929
Thank you.

445
00:29:39,759 --> 00:29:41,629
By the way, how long are they going to do this?

446
00:29:42,029 --> 00:29:43,629
The show is at six o'clock.

447
00:29:44,199 --> 00:29:45,929
They won't even have time to eat.

448
00:29:50,069 --> 00:29:52,679
- What? - Should I pack them lunches?

449
00:29:53,209 --> 00:29:54,909
A support lunch to celebrate their comeback.

450
00:29:55,709 --> 00:29:57,209
You're not cooking it yourself, are you?

451
00:29:57,449 --> 00:29:59,349
Come on, as fan club president,

452
00:29:59,349 --> 00:30:01,779
- I should do at least that much. - No, that's a terrible idea.

453
00:30:01,979 --> 00:30:03,589
You can't even get the water right for ramyeon.

454
00:30:03,649 --> 00:30:05,219
Are you trying to kill them?

455
00:30:07,019 --> 00:30:08,019
Is this all?

456
00:30:08,259 --> 00:30:10,559
You just reused last week's setup and swapped in a new skit.

457
00:30:11,629 --> 00:30:13,759
Is there really a reason to change it up?

458
00:30:13,829 --> 00:30:16,299
If we change things too quickly, the segment won't last as long...

459
00:30:16,369 --> 00:30:17,629
Or is it just that you couldn't write one?

460
00:30:18,899 --> 00:30:19,969
Look...

461
00:30:20,569 --> 00:30:21,899
It's been a month since this segment premiered,

462
00:30:21,969 --> 00:30:23,909
and you haven't changed the setting even once.

463
00:30:24,409 --> 00:30:27,009
Even if not every episode like some teams...

464
00:30:27,009 --> 00:30:28,179
Like Asura?

465
00:30:34,079 --> 00:30:36,449
Understood. I'll rewrite it.

466
00:30:37,189 --> 00:30:38,819
Give me a break.

467
00:30:38,889 --> 00:30:41,289
- Do you have a death wish? - What's this?

468
00:30:41,526 --> 00:30:43,656
- Isn't that a celebrity van? - Looks like it.

469
00:30:49,796 --> 00:30:50,796
Okay.

470
00:30:51,096 --> 00:30:53,266
- Great work. - Great work, everyone.

471
00:30:53,636 --> 00:30:55,906
Hey, we should go running along the Han River sometime.

472
00:30:56,276 --> 00:30:58,936
- Thanks for your hard work. - Thank you, thank you.

473
00:30:59,006 --> 00:31:00,776
Thank you, thank you.

474
00:31:04,476 --> 00:31:06,186
What brings you guys here?

475
00:31:09,316 --> 00:31:11,656
Those must be your bags inside. Man, my bad.

476
00:31:13,126 --> 00:31:14,256
Sorry about that.

477
00:31:15,126 --> 00:31:17,396
The ticket booth looked so deserted...

478
00:31:17,396 --> 00:31:18,996
that I thought there was no show today.

479
00:31:19,596 --> 00:31:20,596
My gosh.

480
00:31:21,626 --> 00:31:22,766
Typical of you.

481
00:31:24,266 --> 00:31:26,306
Did your interview go well?

482
00:31:27,406 --> 00:31:29,236
Yes, it wasn't bad.

483
00:31:30,576 --> 00:31:31,576
Hey.

484
00:31:32,306 --> 00:31:34,906
It really brought back old memories the whole time.

485
00:31:35,406 --> 00:31:37,946
Just to stand on this tiny little stage,

486
00:31:38,316 --> 00:31:40,316
we wandered around handing out flyers...

487
00:31:40,386 --> 00:31:41,516
and doing street performances.

488
00:31:41,586 --> 00:31:44,016
- Gives me chills, seriously. - Tell me about it.

489
00:31:44,086 --> 00:31:45,756
Still, now that it's all in the past,

490
00:31:45,856 --> 00:31:48,156
- it's kind of nostalgic, right? - Totally.

491
00:31:51,056 --> 00:31:52,456
What about you guys?

492
00:31:53,566 --> 00:31:54,996
Is the comeback prep going well?

493
00:31:55,696 --> 00:31:56,796
Actually...

494
00:31:57,466 --> 00:31:59,666
Strictly speaking, is it even a comeback?

495
00:32:00,006 --> 00:32:02,536
Like, a re-debut? What would you call it?

496
00:32:02,606 --> 00:32:05,306
- Kind of vague, right? - It's pretty vague.

497
00:32:05,476 --> 00:32:06,676
Seriously.

498
00:32:07,076 --> 00:32:09,146
Here you are.

499
00:32:10,216 --> 00:32:12,746
I didn't realize you were in here,

500
00:32:12,816 --> 00:32:14,686
so I spent forever searching outside.

501
00:32:14,746 --> 00:32:16,156
So you were in here.

502
00:32:16,216 --> 00:32:18,756
- Surprise! - Another one, seriously.

503
00:32:19,356 --> 00:32:20,626
Give me a break.

504
00:32:21,356 --> 00:32:22,426
That's Hwang Chan Sung, right?

505
00:32:22,696 --> 00:32:23,856
You know, occasionally,

506
00:32:23,856 --> 00:32:25,256
I get fans following me around like that.

507
00:32:25,996 --> 00:32:27,596
- Sorry about that. - Sure.

508
00:32:29,396 --> 00:32:33,736
- Yes, hello, thank you. - You haven't eaten yet, right?

509
00:32:34,106 --> 00:32:36,236
- I packed boxed lunches. - Excuse me.

510
00:32:36,306 --> 00:32:38,906
Wait, why would you make this?

511
00:32:38,976 --> 00:32:42,346
- I mean, who are we for you to... - You really didn't have to.

512
00:32:43,346 --> 00:32:44,376
Thank you.

513
00:32:45,076 --> 00:32:46,086
Thank you so much.

514
00:32:46,146 --> 00:32:47,446
This looks delicious. What's all this?

515
00:32:48,386 --> 00:32:50,556
- Wait, hold on a second. - What's this?

516
00:32:50,916 --> 00:32:53,786
- Hey. Hey, say hello. - What?

517
00:32:53,856 --> 00:32:56,996
This is our fan club president. Our fan club.

518
00:32:57,056 --> 00:32:58,356
(Asura)

519
00:32:59,466 --> 00:33:01,426
Fan club?

520
00:33:03,166 --> 00:33:04,436
Oh, right.

521
00:33:05,836 --> 00:33:09,236
I also packed some snacks separately for the staff.

522
00:33:09,936 --> 00:33:10,936
- Right. - Don't.

523
00:33:11,706 --> 00:33:13,406
- Yes. - No, wait, wait.

524
00:33:16,516 --> 00:33:18,046
- Here is... - No, I'm not on the staff.

525
00:33:18,116 --> 00:33:19,486
- Pardon? - I'm not part of the staff.

526
00:33:21,086 --> 00:33:22,856
- Just... - Take one...

527
00:33:22,916 --> 00:33:24,016
I'm not on the staff.

528
00:33:24,086 --> 00:33:25,716
(Asura's Tenth Anniversary Show)

529
00:33:25,786 --> 00:33:28,126
Served him right. That was so satisfying.

530
00:33:28,256 --> 00:33:30,126
Hey, hold on, wait.

531
00:33:36,266 --> 00:33:37,996
That's so funny. I can't even...

532
00:33:39,266 --> 00:33:41,336
