795
00:46:25,036 --> 00:46:26,436
If you're drunk, just go back up.

796
00:46:26,866 --> 00:46:29,036
No, it's not because I'm drunk.

797
00:46:31,876 --> 00:46:33,546
It's because I'm just so happy.

798
00:46:35,446 --> 00:46:39,546
Being with you, Tae Gu, Jun Seo, and Nam Il...

799
00:46:41,116 --> 00:46:43,156
When we're all together like that,

800
00:46:46,826 --> 00:46:48,756
it's fun and comforting.

801
00:46:51,826 --> 00:46:55,966
"It's safe here, so you can just stay like this."

802
00:46:57,966 --> 00:46:59,766
"You don't need to try so hard."

803
00:47:00,906 --> 00:47:03,576
It feels like someone is telling me that.

804
00:47:06,006 --> 00:47:07,446
So...

805
00:47:09,546 --> 00:47:10,646
Lately...

806
00:47:13,246 --> 00:47:14,386
I truly...

807
00:47:15,786 --> 00:47:17,116
feel so happy.

808
00:47:37,206 --> 00:47:38,206
What is it?

809
00:47:42,446 --> 00:47:43,446
Nothing.

810
00:47:46,686 --> 00:47:47,886
I was just thinking...

811
00:47:50,486 --> 00:47:52,286
that a smile looks much better on you.

812
00:48:03,236 --> 00:48:04,766
Though I've felt this for a while,

813
00:48:05,466 --> 00:48:06,536
you have a knack...

814
00:48:06,536 --> 00:48:08,036
for dropping cheesy lines so casually.

815
00:48:08,936 --> 00:48:10,036
Are you a player?

816
00:48:13,806 --> 00:48:14,846
Me?

817
00:48:16,506 --> 00:48:17,616
You're definitely a player.

818
00:48:19,376 --> 00:48:21,316
The way you suddenly hugged me back then...

819
00:48:22,046 --> 00:48:23,116
Total player.

820
00:48:26,626 --> 00:48:27,626
Aren't they cute?

821
00:48:28,856 --> 00:48:31,526
Everyone else knows, and they're the only two who don't.

822
00:48:32,256 --> 00:48:33,566
So cute.

823
00:48:38,836 --> 00:48:41,466
Are you really playing matchmaker for your friend now?

824
00:48:43,506 --> 00:48:45,536
Instead of worrying about his love life,

825
00:48:45,706 --> 00:48:48,106
how about taking care of your own for once?

826
00:48:52,276 --> 00:48:54,086
- Excuse me. - Yes?

827
00:48:54,746 --> 00:48:56,186
Let me make this crystal clear.

828
00:48:56,856 --> 00:48:58,316
You're not my type.

829
00:48:59,986 --> 00:49:01,186
Stop wasting your time.

830
00:49:08,366 --> 00:49:10,396
Then what kind of girl do you like?

831
00:49:11,596 --> 00:49:12,596
Sweetheart.

832
00:49:13,166 --> 00:49:14,236
Jun Seo.

833
00:49:15,106 --> 00:49:16,366
Babe.

834
00:49:18,976 --> 00:49:20,006
He's not buying it.

835
00:49:21,806 --> 00:49:23,316
Playing hard to get, are we?

836
00:49:23,876 --> 00:49:25,146
Well, then...

837
00:49:25,746 --> 00:49:27,716
Looks like drastic measures are in order.

838
00:49:29,286 --> 00:49:31,586
(Comedy Town)

839
00:49:34,656 --> 00:49:35,756
- Gosh, you scared me. - Hey.

840
00:49:38,196 --> 00:49:39,196
If...

841
00:49:39,796 --> 00:49:41,466
this sketch is a hit,

842
00:49:43,896 --> 00:49:45,536
I'm going to propose to Na Yeon.

843
00:49:47,466 --> 00:49:50,636
Where should we get our newlywed home?

844
00:49:52,636 --> 00:49:54,346
What neighborhood is good these days?

845
00:49:54,576 --> 00:49:55,576
Hey.

846
00:49:56,246 --> 00:49:57,846
If you don't want to end up living with us,

847
00:49:57,916 --> 00:49:59,646
just memorize your lines properly, drama queen.

848
00:49:59,716 --> 00:50:01,086
- You punk, hey... - What?

849
00:50:01,146 --> 00:50:02,786
- Don't jinx it. Take it back. - Take back what?

850
00:50:02,786 --> 00:50:03,986
- Take it back. Spit three times. - Take what back?

851
00:50:03,986 --> 00:50:05,856
- Take it back, you jerk. - Take what back?

852
00:50:05,856 --> 00:50:07,056
- You... - Guys.

853
00:50:08,686 --> 00:50:11,126
- Why is this guy always running? - Well...

854
00:50:11,896 --> 00:50:12,896
I think you need to see this.

855
00:50:12,956 --> 00:50:14,996
- What is it? - Poured it.

856
00:50:15,066 --> 00:50:18,636
Now, timid and nervous.

857
00:50:19,366 --> 00:50:22,306
Timid, timid, nervous, nervous. No. You can do it.

858
00:50:22,406 --> 00:50:24,636
You can do it. You got this.

859
00:50:24,736 --> 00:50:27,976
- Don't keep getting so bold. - When is it coming out?

860
00:50:29,746 --> 00:50:32,416
Is this how you run a business? I can do it.

861
00:50:33,116 --> 00:50:34,546
Goodness, I'm sorry.

862
00:50:34,716 --> 00:50:35,816
There's still more.

863
00:50:36,786 --> 00:50:38,556
I'm so sorry. I'm sorry...

864
00:50:38,756 --> 00:50:40,256
That's business.

865
00:50:47,866 --> 00:50:52,396
(The Kind Chan Sung)

866
00:51:01,706 --> 00:51:03,046
He totally ripped us off.

867
00:51:04,916 --> 00:51:06,216
- Even the punchline is identical. - Hwang Chan Sung!

868
00:51:06,276 --> 00:51:07,346
(Punchline: The ending, twist, or climax of a story,)

869
00:51:07,416 --> 00:51:08,546
(the key scene that delivers the biggest laugh)

870
00:51:08,616 --> 00:51:10,416
This is a straight-up copy-and-paste.

871
00:51:11,156 --> 00:51:12,186
What are you going to do?

872
00:51:16,686 --> 00:51:18,426
It's not like our name is written on an idea,

873
00:51:19,396 --> 00:51:20,866
and if he claims he came up with it first,

874
00:51:20,926 --> 00:51:22,266
there's nothing we can do.

875
00:51:22,896 --> 00:51:25,136
That's what happened before when he stole Tae Gu's sketch.

876
00:51:26,936 --> 00:51:29,666
After all the work we put into that sketch, what now?

877
00:51:33,276 --> 00:51:34,376
Unbelievable.

878
00:51:37,146 --> 00:51:38,376
Where are you going?

879
00:51:39,346 --> 00:51:40,346
To catch a thief.

880
00:51:41,316 --> 00:51:42,416
And do what?

881
00:51:42,986 --> 00:51:44,656
Do you think he'll admit it after it already aired?

882
00:51:44,716 --> 00:51:46,156
I should at least let him know...

883
00:51:47,056 --> 00:51:48,286
what kind of crap he pulled.

884
00:51:55,766 --> 00:51:57,736
Hey, where are you?

885
00:52:07,476 --> 00:52:08,546
Why did you do it?

886
00:52:10,716 --> 00:52:12,216
- Do what? - Don't play dumb...

887
00:52:12,216 --> 00:52:13,216
when we both already know.

888
00:52:13,816 --> 00:52:14,886
Your new sketch...

889
00:52:17,456 --> 00:52:18,456
That's ours.

890
00:52:19,586 --> 00:52:20,756
What?

891
00:52:23,926 --> 00:52:25,656
Hey, what kind of ridiculous nonsense...

892
00:52:28,926 --> 00:52:30,066
Are things that tough for you?

893
00:52:30,396 --> 00:52:33,236
You should just ask me for help instead, Tae Gu.

894
00:52:37,036 --> 00:52:38,036
Want me to show you the proof?

895
00:52:40,206 --> 00:52:41,206
Just say the word.

896
00:52:41,446 --> 00:52:43,216
I have the file from our first brainstorm,

897
00:52:43,746 --> 00:52:45,376
down to the rehearsal videos.

898
00:52:51,886 --> 00:52:54,126
I've got a million curses on the tip of my tongue,

899
00:52:55,656 --> 00:52:56,756
but putting all that aside,

900
00:52:57,596 --> 00:52:59,196
let me ask you comic to comic.

901
00:53:02,496 --> 00:53:03,966
Do you really enjoy performing that?

902
00:53:06,296 --> 00:53:07,336
That material...

903
00:53:08,266 --> 00:53:09,836
isn't fit for who you are.

904
00:53:11,676 --> 00:53:12,976
Faking it on stage like that,

905
00:53:13,046 --> 00:53:14,376
how long do you think you can keep it up?

906
00:53:15,476 --> 00:53:16,776
It's not even fun for you.

907
00:53:18,216 --> 00:53:19,216
Am I wrong?

908
00:53:22,416 --> 00:53:25,886
Here we go again, whining about having fun.

909
00:53:27,156 --> 00:53:28,486
Why do you never change?

910
00:53:29,826 --> 00:53:30,826
Fine.

911
00:53:32,396 --> 00:53:34,466
Let's say I copied it, just like you say.

912
00:53:35,096 --> 00:53:36,536
What difference does that make?

913
00:53:38,236 --> 00:53:40,206
No matter how many times you guys audition,

914
00:53:40,266 --> 00:53:42,466
it never gets approved, not even this sketch.

915
00:53:43,306 --> 00:53:45,076
If you took it in, it would get rejected.

916
00:53:45,136 --> 00:53:46,406
Only because it was me...

917
00:53:48,246 --> 00:53:49,376
did it get the green light.

918
00:53:50,846 --> 00:53:52,746
- What? - And what did you just say earlier?

919
00:53:52,746 --> 00:53:54,486
Proof? Give me a break.

920
00:53:55,716 --> 00:53:56,786
Go ahead, show it.

921
00:53:57,756 --> 00:53:59,186
If I deny it to the end,

922
00:53:59,186 --> 00:54:01,686
will the network take your side, or mine?

923
00:54:01,686 --> 00:54:03,226
Snap out of it!

924
00:54:13,266 --> 00:54:14,406
Making a scene like this...

925
00:54:14,506 --> 00:54:17,106
will only end up hurting you guys, and you should know that, Tae Gu.

926
00:54:25,316 --> 00:54:26,686
How did you end up like this?

927
00:54:29,216 --> 00:54:30,316
Aren't you ashamed of yourself?

928
00:54:34,956 --> 00:54:36,226
Hey, ask anyone walking down...

929
00:54:38,796 --> 00:54:40,596
Grab 100 people off the street and ask them.

930
00:54:40,666 --> 00:54:41,766
Between you...

931
00:54:44,336 --> 00:54:45,366
and me right now,

932
00:54:46,506 --> 00:54:48,706
who looks more pathetic?

933
00:54:49,136 --> 00:54:51,276
Shame on you.

934
00:54:53,276 --> 00:54:55,506
I'm leaving. I have a schedule.

935
00:55:29,276 --> 00:55:30,276
Yes?

936
00:55:30,776 --> 00:55:33,016
- Excuse me. - Oh, wait...

937
00:55:34,746 --> 00:55:35,816
Seriously...

938
00:55:37,556 --> 00:55:39,386
Hello.

939
00:55:39,926 --> 00:55:42,356
How long have you recognized me?

940
00:55:53,736 --> 00:55:56,776
I'm kind of in a hurry right now, so...

941
00:55:57,306 --> 00:55:58,336
I...

942
00:56:01,346 --> 00:56:03,846
What do you think you're doing?

943
00:56:08,786 --> 00:56:10,416
What's wrong with you? Wait...

944
00:56:12,016 --> 00:56:13,286
Are you crazy?

945
00:56:18,026 --> 00:56:19,026
What's this?

946
00:56:19,426 --> 00:56:21,666
Seriously, this woman is out of her mind.

947
00:56:30,536 --> 00:56:31,576
Go ahead, try it.

948
00:56:37,816 --> 00:56:38,876
Darn it.

949
00:56:42,816 --> 00:56:44,916
Hey, I'm not letting this slide.

950
00:56:44,986 --> 00:56:46,686
I'm pressing charges against this crazy woman.

951
00:56:46,756 --> 00:56:47,786
Take the sketch.

952
00:56:50,856 --> 00:56:51,856
What?

953
00:56:52,626 --> 00:56:54,226
I was furious earlier,

954
00:56:54,226 --> 00:56:55,666
so I wanted to take this all the way...

955
00:56:57,896 --> 00:56:59,166
But seeing how pathetic you look right now,

956
00:57:00,506 --> 00:57:01,766
I feel bad for you, so I'll just give it to you.

957
00:57:03,706 --> 00:57:08,076
Just take it. Just remember one thing.

958
00:57:09,746 --> 00:57:11,216
The moment you stole what was mine,

959
00:57:13,986 --> 00:57:15,886
you lost to me for the rest of your life.

960
00:57:33,166 --> 00:57:34,606
Where are you, you idiot?

961
00:57:35,136 --> 00:57:37,506
Get over here right now! You idiot...

962
00:57:40,846 --> 00:57:41,846
Darn it!

963
00:57:51,456 --> 00:57:53,116
Why are you so fearless?

964
00:57:53,886 --> 00:57:56,456
In all my life, I haven't met a woman more reckless than me.

965
00:57:56,826 --> 00:57:59,726
- Reckless, and completely fearless. - I...

966
00:58:00,596 --> 00:58:02,896
I just wanted to protect you.

967
00:58:03,296 --> 00:58:05,966
As the president of the Asura fan club,

968
00:58:06,036 --> 00:58:08,966
- I couldn't just stand by. - There you go again.

969
00:58:09,366 --> 00:58:12,206
You're the only member. What "president" nonsense is that?

970
00:58:14,346 --> 00:58:17,446
- You really drive me crazy. - Cut it out, man.

971
00:58:17,946 --> 00:58:20,586
If you were worried, just say so. Why get so angry?

972
00:58:21,286 --> 00:58:22,816
It's not like that at all, Mr. Man Sik.

973
00:58:23,486 --> 00:58:26,656
"Not like that at all"? Nonsense. Stop it, kid.

974
00:58:26,726 --> 00:58:28,056
You're scaring all the customers away.

975
00:58:28,456 --> 00:58:30,096
Anyway, speaking of which...

976
00:58:30,296 --> 00:58:31,896
Are you really giving up on the sketch now?

977
00:58:32,656 --> 00:58:33,726
We don't have a choice.

978
00:58:34,226 --> 00:58:35,596
Like he said, as long as he denies it,

979
00:58:35,596 --> 00:58:37,396
the network will take his side.

980
00:58:37,966 --> 00:58:39,696
That's just how this business is.

981
00:58:39,966 --> 00:58:41,366
If you don't like it, you just have to succeed.

982
00:58:42,166 --> 00:58:45,376
Still, our club president got revenge for us,

983
00:58:46,946 --> 00:58:48,146
so he won't dare mess with us again.

984
00:58:51,416 --> 00:58:52,416
Are you smiling?

985
00:58:53,886 --> 00:58:54,886
No.

986
00:58:58,616 --> 00:59:01,056
Oh, right. I noticed we're out of onions.

987
00:59:01,126 --> 00:59:02,356
I'll go buy some before it gets busy.

988
00:59:02,426 --> 00:59:05,626
No. Don't worry about it. The new part-timer will get them.

989
00:59:07,266 --> 00:59:08,466
You found a part-timer?

990
00:59:08,996 --> 00:59:09,996
I thought you said there were none.

991
00:59:10,066 --> 00:59:12,396
- Really? Who is it? - I'm here, Boss.

992
00:59:12,466 --> 00:59:13,666
You made it.

993
00:59:14,536 --> 00:59:15,766
You know where the storage is, right?

994
00:59:15,836 --> 00:59:17,806
- Yes. - Just put them there.

995
00:59:18,976 --> 00:59:20,776
- Ji Young. - Hey, Eun Young.

996
00:59:21,306 --> 00:59:23,076
- What are you doing? - Working here.

997
00:59:27,386 --> 00:59:29,246
Wait, you should've discussed this with me.

998
00:59:29,416 --> 00:59:30,916
I'm the one who has to work with her.

999
00:59:31,186 --> 00:59:32,486
If you don't like it, run the place yourself.

1000
00:59:32,756 --> 00:59:34,756
What was I supposed to do? Hyun Seok vanished,

1001
00:59:34,826 --> 00:59:37,196
and you asked to cut your hours to focus on comedy.

1002
00:59:37,556 --> 00:59:38,756
I can't do this alone. You know that.

1003
00:59:39,196 --> 00:59:41,396
No, but still, this is...

1004
00:59:41,666 --> 00:59:43,466
Come on out, everyone.

1005
00:59:44,236 --> 00:59:48,366
Ji Young's initiation ceremony starts right now!

1006
00:59:50,736 --> 00:59:52,276
She wants an initiation. Come on.

1007
00:59:52,736 --> 00:59:54,546
Please take good care of her. Help her out.

1008
00:59:54,976 --> 00:59:56,546
What are you going to do about this?

1009
00:59:58,416 --> 01:00:00,586
Did you see Jun Seo freaking out when he saw me earlier?

1010
01:00:01,816 --> 01:00:02,816
So cute.

1011
01:00:04,656 --> 01:00:06,386
Are you really going to work there?

1012
01:00:07,056 --> 01:00:08,856
- Is that okay? - Why wouldn't it be?

1013
01:00:09,656 --> 01:00:11,696
Do you also think Jun Seo and I don't look good together?

1014
01:00:11,796 --> 01:00:12,996
It's not that.

1015
01:00:13,566 --> 01:00:15,726
You seem to take on random jobs,

1016
01:00:16,396 --> 01:00:18,366
but you never did anything that could ruin your hands.

1017
01:00:22,906 --> 01:00:23,906
What are you talking about?

1018
01:00:24,506 --> 01:00:26,036
It's been forever since I quit piano.

1019
01:00:28,146 --> 01:00:29,776
I never avoided it on purpose.

1020
01:00:30,006 --> 01:00:32,646
It's just that I happened to look for easy jobs.

1021
01:00:34,916 --> 01:00:37,316
Just wait and see. Within three months,

1022
01:00:37,716 --> 01:00:40,456
I'll have Jun Seo following me everywhere.

1023
01:00:40,886 --> 01:00:41,886
You got this.

1024
01:00:43,826 --> 01:00:45,326
You're something else.

1025
01:00:45,796 --> 01:00:46,996
You should make a move too.

1026
01:00:47,396 --> 01:00:48,666
You're going to lose him if you just sit around.

1027
01:00:48,726 --> 01:00:51,066
From what I saw yesterday, Tae Gu is surprisingly popular.

1028
01:00:51,536 --> 01:00:54,966
- Hey, it's really not like that. - Suit yourself.

1029
01:00:55,606 --> 01:00:57,876
Go to sleep first. I'll stretch a bit before bed.

1030
01:00:59,876 --> 01:01:02,876
Seriously, unbelievable.

1031
01:01:03,376 --> 01:01:04,976
I keep telling her it's not like that.

1032
01:01:07,486 --> 01:01:09,816
Seriously, this woman is out of her mind.

1033
01:01:14,086 --> 01:01:15,086
Go ahead, try it.

1034
01:01:22,666 --> 01:01:26,166
You've lost your mind, Go Eun Young. Get a grip. Have some respect.

1035
01:01:27,206 --> 01:01:28,206
Eun Young.

1036
01:01:29,866 --> 01:01:30,976
Did you take your medication today?

1037
01:01:33,006 --> 01:01:35,476
- Oh, right. - But there's none left.

1038
01:01:35,906 --> 01:01:37,516
There are only a few morning pills left.

1039
01:01:38,816 --> 01:01:39,816
Really?

1040
01:01:40,886 --> 01:01:42,486
You can't be doing this.

1041
01:01:42,816 --> 01:01:45,816
Taking your medication regularly is essential for treatment.

1042
01:01:46,386 --> 01:01:47,586
You have to be diligent about it.

1043
01:01:48,956 --> 01:01:51,326
Yes, I'm sorry.

1044
01:01:52,256 --> 01:01:53,456
Still, what's encouraging is that...

1045
01:01:54,096 --> 01:01:55,826
a patient who couldn't get by without medication...

1046
01:01:56,396 --> 01:01:57,996
didn't even realize she had run out.

1047
01:01:59,796 --> 01:02:02,106
It seems you've found something to take its place.

1048
01:02:04,976 --> 01:02:05,976
Yes.

1049
01:02:16,046 --> 01:02:18,116
- I'm sorry. Excuse me for a moment. - Sure.

1050
01:02:19,016 --> 01:02:21,786
Good grief. Of all the times.

1051
01:02:21,986 --> 01:02:22,986
I'm sorry.

1052
01:02:29,896 --> 01:02:30,996
Yes, thank you.

1053
01:02:39,636 --> 01:02:42,046
Gosh. Thank you.

1054
01:02:47,986 --> 01:02:49,316
Seriously.

1055
01:02:50,516 --> 01:02:51,556
I'm sorry.

1056
01:02:52,786 --> 01:02:53,786
Thank you.

1057
01:02:55,286 --> 01:02:57,556
(Hyujung Mental Health Clinic)

1058
